# Apple corners & typography (launcher UI)

In `uclient_launcher_ui.h`, treat **Apple-style** UI as the default for launcher surfaces: **`var(--font-apple-round)`**, generous **`border-radius`** (sheet `var(--sc-r-sheet)`, inset fields `var(--sc-r-inset)`, **pill buttons `999px`**), plus **squircle** where supported.

## Squircle (`corner-shape`)

1. Set `border-radius` on the element (blocks ~26–32px, inset ~18px, pills 999px).
2. Add the selector to the `@supports (corner-shape: squircle)` block in the same edit.

## Must use Apple round + squircle

- **Shortcuts / Automation editor** (`#sc-editor`, `#shortcuts-view`): blocks, drawer, tiles, pills, menus, run results (existing list).
- **Confirm / share dialogs** (`.confirm-layer`, `.confirm-box`, `#confirm-layer`, `#share-link-layer`): modal sheet, optional `.confirm-files` list, **Cancel / Confirm / Discard** and **Copy link** buttons (pill shape).
- **Readonly link fields** in dialogs (e.g. `#share-link-url`).

## Dialog details list

- `#confirm-files` is only for **optional detail lines** (file names, etc.) when `openConfirmDialog(..., details)` passes a non-empty array.
- When there are no details, keep it **`hidden`** and **`display: none`** — never show an empty bordered box.

## When adding new UI

- Reuse `.confirm-box` / `.confirm-actions` patterns instead of one-off modal CSS.
- Do not ship sharp-corner-only panels in the launcher unless squircle is unsupported (fallback remains `border-radius` only).

